{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7634","id":5210514011,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABNpIiWw","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7634","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7634.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7634.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7634","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7634/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7634/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7634/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/statuses/2589f41ddfe6c10b98e573fa793f48294b948f52","number":7634,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix(pm-stack): Meta keeper re-arm restores each unit from its own .backup (#6366)","user":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #6366 (task 12941).\n\n`defaultEnsureExporterArmed` was all-or-nothing: it reported armed only when both Meta quota exporter units existed, restored only when both `.backup` copies existed, and every mixed state fell through to `missing` — whose alert then falsely stated that no `.backup` copies exist. A partial rename (the exact failure family the keeper was built for) could never be recovered.\n\nChanges (`pm-stack/aggregator/src/meta-renewal.ts`):\n- The filesystem implementation is now exported as `ensureExporterArmedForUnitDir(unitDir, afterRestore?)` and handles each unit independently: a present unit stays, a missing unit is restored from its own `.backup` copy, a unit with neither is reported missing. Restoring at least one unit (with the pair ending armed) reports `restored`.\n- New `partial:<per-unit state>` result (e.g. `partial:timer=restored,service=missing`) when at least one unit/backup was found but the pair is not fully armed. The keeper carries it as `exporter-partial:<state>` in `recovery.result`, and the alert names the actual per-unit state instead of claiming no backups exist.\n- The `exporter-missing` alert (no units, no backups) is unchanged for the true-empty case.\n\nTests (`meta-renewal.test.ts`): new suite exercises the default implementation against a fake unit directory — already-armed, both backups, partial backup for each unit, partial-with-missing-other-unit, neither — plus a keeper-level test that the partial alert names per-unit state and never claims no backups exist. Oracle: the filesystem state of the fake unit directory after the call.\n\nVerified on the laptop: `bun test src/meta-renewal.test.ts` — 14 pass, 0 fail.\n\n🤖 Queue worker lane code-e (task 12941)\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796725208&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7634&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7634&signature=56f9e33c00d7620121577d9d4e4e1fc699f253934897179c97a72eccf9e8892c\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7634?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-08T10:20:04Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T10:41:53Z","closed_at":"2026-11-08T10:41:51Z","merged_at":"2026-11-08T10:41:50Z","merge_commit_sha":"25210239f337a1af19554048f2f364d7aec5f3de","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"developing-today:queue/12941-6366-meta-keeper-per-unit","ref":"queue/12941-6366-meta-keeper-per-unit","repo":{"id":627308783,"node_id":"R_kgDOJWP47w","name":"code","full_name":"developing-today/code","owner":{"login":"developing-today","id":26439447,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjI2NDM5NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26439447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today/starred{/owner}{/rep